School Faculty Directory: Hon. Amy Coney Barrett, Professor of Law\". Notre Dame, Indiana: University of Notre Dame School of Law. Archived from the original on April 2, 2019. Retrieved March 14, 2019.\n36. 1 2 3 4 5 6 Howe, Amy (September 21, 2020). \"Profile of a potential nominee: Amy Coney Barrett\". *SCOTUSblog*. Archived from the original on September 23, 2020.\n37. 1 2 Sweet, Lynn; Seidel, Jon (September 24, 2020). \"How Amy Coney Barrett went from Notre Dame to Supreme Court frontrunner\". *Chicago Sun-Times*. Archived from the original on February 14, 2021. Retrieved September 29, 2020.\n38. ↑ Carr, Thomas B. (July 26, 2004). \"Letters to the Editor: 'Now-Defunct' Miller, Cassidy\". *National Law Journal*. Archived from the original on September 30, 2017. Retrieved September 29, 2017. (subscription required)\n39. 1 2 Tomazin, Farrah (September 27, 2020). \"Five things you should know about Trump's Supreme Court nominee Amy Coney Barrett\". *The Sydney Morning Herald*. Archived from the original on February 14, 2021. Retrieved September 27, 2020.\n40. ↑ Andrew Kragie. \"How Amy Coney Barrett Describes Her Legal Career\". *law360.com*. Archived from the original on February 14, 2021. Retrieved October 3, 2020.\n41. 1 2 3 4 \"Hon. Amy Coney Barrett\". University of Notre Dame. Archived from the original on April 2, 2019. Retrieved August 19, 2020.\n42. 1 2 Taylor, Julia (September 28, 2020). \"Judge Amy Coney Barrett: Selected Primary Material\". Congressional Research Service. LSB10539. Archived from the original on February 14, 2021. Retrieved September 30, 2020.\n43. 1 2 Nicholas, Peter; Radnofsky, Louise (July 5, 2018). . *The Wall Street Journal*. Retrieved July 5, 2018.`{{cite news}}`: CS1 maint: deprecated archival service (link)\n44. ↑ Brown, Emma; Swaine, Jon (September 27, 2020). \"Amy Coney Barrett, Supreme Court nominee, spoke at program founded to inspire a 'distinctly Christian worldview in every area of law'\". *The Washington Post*. Retrieved September 29, 2020.\n45. ↑ Sheckler, Christian (September 24, 2020). \"What Amy Coney Barrett's former Notre Dame colleagues say about her\". *The Indianapolis Star*. Retrieved September 27, 2020.\n46. ↑ \"Trump Names 10 Conservatives It Plans to Nominate to Federal Courts\". *Chicago Tribune*. May 8, 2017. Archived from the original on September 30, 2017. Retrieved September 29, 2017.\n47. ↑ \"Rescheduled Notice of Committee Hearing\". Senate Judiciary Committee. August 4, 2017. Archived from the original on October 6, 2017. Retrieved October 7, 2017.\n48. ↑ Barrett, Amy; Garvey, John (January 1, 1998). \"Catholic Judges in Capital Cases\". *Marq. L. Rev*. **81**: 303. Archived from the original on February 14, 2021. Retrieved September 19, 2020.\n49. ↑ Johnson, Eliana. \"How Amy Coney Barrett vaulted onto Trump's Supreme Court shortlist\". *Politico*. Archived from the original on September 23, 2020. Retrieved July 3, 2018.\n50. ↑ \"Judicial and Justice Department Pending Nominations\". C-SPAN. Archived from the original on September 22, 2020. Retrieved September 13, 2020.\n51. 1 2 Gerstein, Josh (September 11, 2017). \"Senators take fire over questions for Catholic judicial nominee\". *Politico*. Archived from the original on June 29, 2018. Retrieved June 30, 2018.\n52. ↑ Freking, Kevin (September 11, 2017). \"Catholics decry Dems' questioning of judicial pick\". *The Detroit News*. Associated Press. Archived from the original on February 14, 2021. Retrieved September 27, 2020.\n53. ↑ Green, Emma (September 8, 2017). \"Should a Judge's Nomination Be Derailed by Her Faith?\". *The Atlantic*. Archived from the original on June 30, 2018. Retrieved July 1, 2018.\n54. 1 2 Goodstein, Laurie (September 28, 2017). \"Some Worry About Judicial Nominee's Ties to a Religious Group\". *The New York Times*. Retrieved July 4, 2018.`{{cite news}}`: CS1 maint: deprecated archival service (link)\n55. ↑ \"Feinstein: 'The dogma lives loudly within you, and that is a concern'\". *The 